          "character": 1
        }
      },
      "title": "ML 1. Context features: what the shape alone cannot see",
      "description": "For every transfer we compute 20 numbers the model learns from (`graph_features`):\n\n* **KYC**: account type (NGO, business, merchant, personal), account age, **same owner** (line 108)\n* **Pass through** (line 117): does the receiver move the money on within 48 hours? Smurf collectors and mules do; NGOs and shops do not\n* **Recurring** (line 125): have these two paid each other before? Payroll and chit funds repeat every month\n* Bursts, similar amounts, just under ₹10,000, round amounts\n\n**SAY:** \"The shape tells us something unusual happened. These features tell us the context: who the accounts are, where the money goes next, and whether it repeats.\""
    },
    {
      "file": "src/features.py",
      "line": 134,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 134,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 155,
          "character": 1
        }
      },
      "title": "ML 2. Combining rules + ML (hybrid)",
      "description": "`rule_features` turns the output of our rule detectors into 8 more inputs for the model: did a rule fire, which shape, its risk score and strength, are the accounts in any alert, and the classic threshold rule flags.\n\nSo the model learns from **both** the rules and the context.\n\n**SAY:** \"We did not throw away the rule engine. Its answers become inputs to the ML model. That is our hybrid.\""
    },
    {
      "file": "src/train_model.py",
      "line": 74,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 72,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 77,
          "character": 1
        }
      },
      "title": "ML 3. Separate training and test data",
      "description": "We split by **date**, never shuffled, because a bank trains on the past and is used on the future:\n\n* **Train**: 1 Jan to 28 Feb (31,480 transfers) → `data/train.csv`\n* **Validation**: last 2 weeks of train, used only to pick the alert threshold\n* **Test**: 1 to 31 Mar (15,937 transfers) → `data/test.csv`, never seen in training\n\n**SAY:** \"Our test month was never seen while training, so the scores are honest.\""
    },
    {
      "file": "src/train_model.py",
      "line": 94,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 46,
