        }
      },
      "title": "ML 6. Explaining the verdict: genuine or laundering?",
      "description": "`signals` writes the evidence in plain English, with ✓ for genuine and ⚠ for laundering, for example:\n\n* ✓ \"ACC00806 is a registered NGO, open for 8 years\"\n* ✓ \"ACC00806 kept the money: none of it moved on within 48 hours\"\n* ✓ \"Every account in the chain belongs to the same customer\"\n* ✓ \"The money went back to someone who had paid in: a rotating savings pool (chit fund)\"\n* ⚠ \"100% of the money collected left the account within 48 hours\"\n\n**SAY:** \"This answers the key question: how do we tell a donation drive from smurfing? The NGO keeps the money and is long established; the smurf collector is new and empties the account within hours.\""
    },
